<title>SOUTH AFRICA: AMCOAL YEAR EPS RISES 30 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>AMCOAL YEAR EPS RISES 30 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     3,459.8     vs 2,662.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 1,320.0     vs 1,000.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   901.28	vs 672.59</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1,367.50    vs 1,030.49</p>
<p>    Tax			 464.98	vs 357.91</p>
<p>    Interest income	 312.82	vs 191.17</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3,285.38    vs 2,748.26</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast a consensus</p>
<p>earnings per share of 3,408.15 cents in a range of 3,200.00</p>
<p>cents to 3,500.00 cents. Analysts reached a dividend consensus</p>
<p>of 1,352.50 cents in a range of 1,260.00 cents and 1,400 cents.</p>
</text>
